Responsive design refers to creating a webpage that looks and functions well on different devices and screen sizes. HTML, CSS, and media queries play a crucial role in designing a responsive webpage. Here are some examples of using HTML, CSS, and media queries to create a responsive design:

1. A simple responsive HTML template using viewport and flexible grids:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .row::after {
            content: "";
            clear: both;
            display: table;
        }
        [class*="col-"] {
            float: left;
            padding: 15px;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .col-1 {width: 8.33%;}
        .col-2 {width: 16.66%;}
        .col-3 {width: 25%;}
        // Add more column widths as needed
    </style>
</head>
